<BaseLayout title="File server backup and recovery" description="How Nova Corp protects departmental data with Windows Server Backup and proves restoration." breadcrumbs={[{label:"NOVA-FILES01",href:"systems/nova-files01/"},{label:"Backup and recovery"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">File server / Windows Server Backup</div><h1>Backup and recovery</h1><p class="lead">The company can recover documents from a separate Windows backup target when a suitable recovery point exists.</p></div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container"><FileRecovery start="backup" /></div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container grid-main"><article class="prose">
<h2>What does the backup protect?</h2><p>The documented Windows Server Backup policy protects the NovaData volume (D:) to NovaBackup (B:) using a daily 22:00 VSS Copy Backup schedule. It does not include bare-metal or System State recovery for this file server.</p>
<Files01DocumentImages ids={["fileserver-backup-gui","fileserver-backup-schedule"]}/>
<h2>Why does the company need it?</h2><h3 class="file-problem">Problem</h3><p>Imagine an employee deletes a report and discovers that no suitable Previous Version is available. IT needs another copy of the document and must be able to restore it rather than merely confirm that backups exist.</p><h3 class="file-solution">Solution</h3><p>I configured Windows Server Backup to retain copies of the data drive on B:. When a document goes missing, IT can select an available backup, restore the file to a separate location and check that the recovered contents match before returning it to the employee.</p>
<h2>How I tested the automatic backup</h2><p>During the scheduled backup test, I first tried Start-ScheduledTask on the built-in Windows Backup task. Windows refused because the task could not start on demand. An attempt to change the schedule while re-adding B: also failed because the target was already registered. The corrected acceptance test changed only the schedule. The following historical commands change configuration; they are not routine diagnostics:</p>
<pre><code>{'$TestTime = (Get-Date).AddMinutes(5).ToString("HH:mm")\nwbadmin enable backup -schedule:$TestTime -quiet'}</code></pre>
<p><strong>Expected:</strong> The scheduled task launches naturally and the backup completes, without a manual wbadmin start backup command.</p><p><strong>Actual:</strong> The journal records a start at 18:17:05, success at 18:17:19, and completion. The normal schedule was restored afterward.</p>
<Files01DocumentImages ids={["fileserver-scheduled-backup-pass"]}/>
<pre><code>wbadmin enable backup -schedule:22:00 -quiet
wbadmin enable backup</code></pre>
<p>The recorded schedule was verified as 22:00 again. For a read-only recovery-point inspection, the journal used <code>wbadmin get versions -backupTarget:B:</code>.</p>
<h2>How I tested file recovery</h2><p>I restored a deleted file to an alternate path and compared SHA-256 fingerprints. The source remained absent from its live Finance location while the recovered file matched the original bytes. A separate controlled exercise took the backup disk offline, repaired it, ran a fresh backup and verified a recovered file.</p>
<Files01DocumentImages ids={["backup-original-recovered-hash","backup-disk-offline","backup-file-recovery","backup-sha256-match"]}/>
<details><summary>Technical checks · read-only verification</summary><p>Run these read-only checks to see the same facts yourself.</p><h3>Enumerate recovery points</h3><p><strong>Run on:</strong> NOVA-FILES01 (elevated PowerShell)</p><pre><code>wbadmin get versions -backupTarget:B:</code></pre><p><strong>Expected:</strong> A valid catalog and available recovery versions; this does not prove that a restore will succeed.</p><h3>Inspect backup target</h3><p><strong>Run on:</strong> NOVA-FILES01</p><pre><code>Get-Volume -DriveLetter B</code></pre><p><strong>Expected:</strong> B: is present with the recorded NovaBackup label and available capacity.</p></details><h2>Related incident and recovery limits</h2><p><a href={base+"incidents/backup-target-unavailable/"}>Read the controlled backup-target failure →</a></p><p>B: is an attached Windows backup volume, separate from D:, kept on a separate hard drive outside the lab. A successful file restore does not prove a complete server or Domain Controller restoration.</p><p><a href={base+"files/shadow-copies/"}>Compare Shadow Copies and Previous Versions →</a></p>
<h2>Engineering journals</h2><p><a href={base+"journals/CR-012_Windows_Server_Backup_and_Recovery_Journal/"}>CR-012 original journal, including scheduled-run acceptance →</a></p><p><a href={base+"journals/Nova_Corp_CR-014_Engineering_Journal_and_Evidence/"}>CR-014 original incident journal →</a></p>
</article><aside><div class="sidebox"><h3>Recorded configuration</h3><dl class="fact-list"><div><dt>Source</dt><dd>D: NovaData</dd></div><div><dt>Target</dt><dd>B: NovaBackup</dd></div><div><dt>Schedule</dt><dd>Daily 22:00</dd></div><div><dt>Mode</dt><dd>VSS Copy Backup</dd></div></dl><p><a href={base+"files/volumes/"}>View storage volumes →</a></p><p><a href={base+"systems/nova-files01/"}>Back to NOVA-FILES01 →</a></p></div></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
